%% Authoritative editable source for the hybrid request-flow diagram.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    box rgb(17,40,65) Client
        participant U as User / client
    end
    box rgb(18,52,46) Trusted orchestration / control plane
        participant F as Hosted Skill + worker
        participant S as Hybrid setup
        participant A as MAF agent
        participant W as Local-tool middleware
    end
    box rgb(16,52,82) Governed external services
        participant G as APIM AI Gateway
        participant M as Foundry model
        participant R as Remote MCP
    end
    box rgb(43,43,36) Customer isolation boundary
        participant X as ACA sandbox<br/>journal + executor + tools
    end
    box rgb(36,35,63) Observability
        participant I as Application Insights
    end

    U->>F: POST agent request
    activate F
    F->>S: Begin top-level hybrid invocation
    activate S
    S->>X: Create one fresh customer sandbox
    S->>X: Prepare package, executor, and manifest
    Note over S,X: Upload selected app or explicit bundle<br/>Verify SHA-256, start persistent executor, discover exact manifest
    X-->>F: Manifest returned, build inert stubs + provenance
    deactivate S

    F->>A: Construct MAF agent and start turn
    activate A
    A->>G: Responses API planning
    G->>M: Managed-identity model call
    M-->>A: Tool plan returned through APIM

    par Remote MCP stays worker-side
        A->>G: Remote MCP tool request
        G->>R: Governed MCP operation
        R-->>A: Read-only result returned through APIM
    and Exact local stubs enter sandbox lane
        A->>W: Invoke exact sandbox-generated stub
        activate W
        W->>X: Execute through no-ingress file journal
        Note over W,X: Strict JSON + idempotent call_id<br/>One shared executor queues tool, shell, file, and search calls
        X-->>A: Result + timings returned through middleware
        deactivate W
    end
    Note over A,X: One turn may select MCP + local calls, local calls share one queued executor

    A->>G: Responses API final synthesis
    G->>M: Managed-identity model call
    M-->>A: Final answer returned through APIM
    deactivate A

    F->>X: Stop, drain, shutdown marker, terminal 300/600 lifecycle
    F->>X: Request handle delete with 5s acceptance bound
    alt Accepted or already absent
        X-->>F: Accepted / NotFound, do not await LRO
    else Pre-acceptance stall or failure
        F->>X: Bounded exact-ID provider delete fallback
        X-->>F: Confirmed deletion / NotFound
    end
    X-->>F: Final typed inventory = 0
    F-->>U: Return completed agent response
    deactivate F

    Note over F,I: W3C correlation spans Functions + APIM<br/>Content-free hybrid progress and metrics flow to Application Insights
    Note over F,A: Model/MCP credentials and clients stay in Functions
    Note over X: Customer identity, deny-by-default egress, no public ingress
    Note over F,X: Only local executables enter ACA, lifecycle + reaper remain backstops
